From: Hexagon toolchain buildroot
Date: Sat, 12 Jul 2026 00:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] rusticl: explicitly allowlist the pipe_map_flags enum for bindgen

RustiCL's meson bindgen arguments mark pipe_map_flags as a --bitfield-enum but,
unlike every other gallium enum used from Rust (pipe_endian, pipe_query_type,
pipe_resource_usage, ...), never pass --allowlist-type for it. It is therefore
only emitted when bindgen happens to reach it transitively from another
allowlisted declaration. On some targets (e.g. hexagon) it is not reached, so
the generated bindings lack the pipe_map_flags newtype and RustiCL fails to
build with "cannot find module or crate pipe_map_flags".

Allowlist the type explicitly, matching the other gallium enums.

Signed-off-by: Hexagon toolchain buildroot
--- a/src/gallium/frontends/rusticl/meson.build
+++ b/src/gallium/frontends/rusticl/meson.build
@@ -315,6 +315,7 @@
     '--allowlist-function',     'pipe_.*',
     '--allowlist-var',          'PIPE_.*',
     '--allowlist-type',         'pipe_endian',
+    '--allowlist-type',         'pipe_map_flags',
     '--bitfield-enum',          'pipe_map_flags',
     '--allowlist-type',         'pipe_query_type',
     '--constified-enum-module', 'pipe_query_type',
